> give penny to clerk
The clerk drops the penny in the till. "You have 1 pence with me."
> give sixpence to clerk
The clerk drops the sixpence in the till. "You have 7 pence with me."
> give red parcel to clerk
"I can't take that over the counter."
> buy 3
The clerk tears off 3 stamps. "4 pence left."
> buy 10
"That's 10 pence. You have 4 with me."
> buy 0
"How many?"
> buy 2 stamps
The clerk tears off 2 stamps. "2 pence left."
> ask clerk about stamps
"Penny a stamp. One for a letter, one more for each band."
> ask clerk about weather
The clerk shrugs.
> clerk, weigh red parcel
The clerk weighs the red parcel: 1 ounces, a letter, 1 stamps.
> clerk, take parcel
The clerk shakes his head.
